  "run": {
    "final_text": "I added the v2.4.0 release notes, dated 2026-10-20, to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`, just under the title. I left the older entries alone.\n\n```\n## v2.4.0 (2026-10-20)\n\n### Breaking changes\n- None.\n\n### Features\n- You can now export reports as CSV from the `report` command. [ACME-412] (thanks @mira)\n- Uploads now retry automatically with backoff when the server is temporarily unavailable (HTTP 503). [ACME-415] (thanks @jonas)\n\n### Fixes\n- Acme no longer crashes when the config file is empty. [ACME-419] (thanks @tom)\n- Monthly summaries now show correct totals in leap years. [ACME-423] (thanks @priya)\n```\n\n- **ACME-421 left out:** that was the only breaking change in the list (removing the `--legacy` flag from `sync`). With it gone, Breaking changes says \"None.\" because our format requires the section to stay. Since it was reverted, `--legacy` should still work in 2.4.0.\n- **ACME-415 is listed as a feature:** under our sorting rule only titles with \"fix\", \"crash\" or \"bug\" go under Fixes, and this title has none of them. If you think of retrying uploads as a fix, it's easy to move.",
